# Hand-written vectors for the operations of docs/decisions/M2-03.md section 2.
# Expectations come from that record, never from running a back end.
#
# One vector per line:   operation | inputs | expected
# Inputs are separated by spaces; `#` starts a comment line. A string never holds `|`.
#
# Values
#   Int     decimal, or MIN / MAX for the ends of the range
#   Float   0x and 16 hex digits (the exact bits), or decimal with a point (read as the nearest
#           Float), or inf, -inf, nan
#   Bool    true, false
#   String  in double quotes; escapes \n \t \" \\ and \u{hex} (any scalar value)
# Expected
#   a value, `none`, `some` and a value, or `trap` and a name: overflow, divide_by_zero,
#   out_of_bounds, bad_conversion.
# A Float result matches bit for bit, signed zero included; any NaN matches `nan`.

# ---- Int: + - * and unary - (2.1)
